==Russian==
{{wikipedia|lang=ru}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|lang=ru|[nɐˈɡa]}}
* {{audio|Ru-нога.ogg|Audio|lang=ru}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|sla-pro|ru}} {{m|sla-pro|*noga}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ru}} {{m|ine-pro|*h₃nogʰ-}}. ‘claw, nail’. Cognate with English ''[[nail]]'', Latvian ''[[nagas]]'', Persian {{term|ناخن|tr=nâxon|lang=fa}}, Latin ''[[unguis]]'', Spanish ''[[uña]]'', Welsh ''[[ewin]]''.

===Noun===
{{ru-noun|нога́|f-in|ноги́|но́ги}}

# [[leg]]
# [[foot]]

====Usage notes====
* Pronunciation of the genitive plural [[ног]] as “нох” is considered old-fashioned.

====Declension====
{{ru-noun-table|6|но́г|а}}

===See also===
* {{l|ru|ступня́}}

===Related terms===
* {{l|ru|безно́гий}}
* {{l|ru|нога́стый}}
* {{l|ru|ножно́й}}
* {{l|ru|одноно́гий}}
* {{l|ru|трено́жник}}

